  "tutorials": [
    {
      "x": 650,
      "text": "Q  asks him to wait. Press Q again to call him back."
    },
    {
      "x": 2040,
      "text": "The gate needs weight on the plate. Ask him to wait [Q], or push the crate onto it."
    },
    {
      "x": 2670,
      "text": "Release the latch [E] on this side. Then call him through [Q]."
    },
    {
      "x": 1050,
      "text": "The stream has taken the crossing. Hold E at the winch to lower it."
    },
    {
      "x": 7350,
      "text": "The loading roof can be made safe. Or watch the dust and time your way through."
    },
    {
      "x": 9560,
      "text": "The gully carries every gust. There is room for both of you behind the fallen trunk."
    },
    {
      "x": 11820,
      "text": "Two ways: the water below, or the boards above. One piece of salvage can make either way safer."
    },
    {
      "x": 12130,
      "text": "Jump onto the upper boards to climb. Keep walking underneath to take the lower way."
    },
    {
      "x": 12230,
      "text": "Someone listens beyond the canal. Running, moving crates and splashing carry. Crouch in the water to keep both of you quiet."
    },
    {
      "x": 15600,
      "text": "The bridge and the mill gate are still joined by the old chain."
    },
    {
      "x": 16200,
      "text": "Jump up the boards. The wheel’s weight can pull the gate. Keep a way back for him."
    },
    {
      "x": 16600,
      "text": "The frame is giving way. Get both children clear when the chain begins to strain."
    }
  ],
